WEBVTT

00:06:58.247 --> 00:07:00.916
that you would use for fuel here on Earth.

00:07:00.916 --> 00:07:03.669
So we'll be examining this
with the Webb telescope

00:07:03.711 --> 00:07:05.546
and we'll be sending a probe out there

00:07:05.546 --> 00:07:09.091
to land with even a helicopter
to go exploring.

00:07:09.091 --> 00:07:11.510
So is this a place
that's interesting for life?

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.678
Possibly.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.013
People ask me all the time,

00:07:14.054 --> 00:07:17.057
are we sure that the kind
we have here is the only kind?

00:07:17.099 --> 00:07:18.309
Well, maybe not.

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:21.395
And if not, this is a good place
to look because it's different,

00:07:21.395 --> 00:07:23.856
but it still has solids,
liquids and gases,

00:07:23.856 --> 00:07:27.401
and it has a liquid hydrocarbon,
which might be a possible solvent.

00:07:27.443 --> 00:07:28.611
We'll see.

00:07:28.611 --> 00:07:30.196
Next thing we want to look at is,